# DISABLED 2026-09-13 — DEFECT_LEDGER #17. Do not restore without reading it.
#
# This drop-in routed every chat turn through the Headroom compressor and handed the
# GENERATOR the compressed text. At production scale it removed 44.9% of tokens by deleting
# short "low-information" words, which on a factual corpus are the facts:
#
#   "Ti" 8 -> 2     the word "two" 6 -> 4     "RTX 5060 Ti" 3 -> 1
#   bare "RTX 5060" (a device that does not exist on this fleet) 0 -> 2
#
#   "on the **RTX 5060 Ti 16 GB** in the asrock B550"   ->  "on **RTX 5060 16 in B550"
#   "the complete GPU inventory: two A4500s and one 5060 Ti."  ->  "inventory: A4500s one 5060 Ti."
#
# It also mangled the GROUNDING rules in SYSTEM_PREFIX and broke the FOLLOWUPS scaffold.
# Live effect: 12/18 answers named a nonexistent RTX 5060, vs 0/16 with the same chunks
# uncompressed.
#
# It bought nothing: MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS is 14,384 and a real prompt is ~2,982 tokens, so the
# budget was never tight; tokens are free on owned hardware; it added ~1,017 ms mean latency;
# and it rewrote the prefix that prefix caching depends on.
#
# To restore it you would first need an integrity gate on device names and numerals. saved_pct
# is not a quality metric.
#
# [Service]
# Environment=COMPRESS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8788
# Environment=COMPRESS_TIMEOUT=15
